# Technical Specifications

## 1. System Overview

Nexora uses an **FPGA + ESP32 architecture** for real-time accident detection and emergency alerting.
  

## 2. Main Components

| Component            | Role                           | Interface      |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------- |
| **Nexys 4 DDR FPGA** | Accident processing & decision | Digital / UART |
| **ESP32**            | Communication gateway          | UART           |
| **Shock Sensor**     | Impact detection               | Digital        |
| **MPU6050**          | Acceleration & motion sensing  | I²C            |
| **NEO-6M GPS**       | Location acquisition           | UART           |
| **SIM800L GSM**      | Emergency SMS                  | UART           |


## 3. FPGA Processing

The FPGA performs the time-critical accident logic:

```
Sensor Inputs
     ↓
Impact Validation
     ↓
Risk Classification
     ↓
Accident FSM
     ↓
Accident Event
     ↓
UART → ESP32
```

### Key Parameters

| Parameter         |            Value |
| ----------------- | ---------------: |
| Validation window |       **250 ms** |
| Impact criterion  |          **70%** |
| Decision logic    | **Accident FSM** |
| FPGA HDL          |      **Verilog** |


## 4. ESP32 Communication

The ESP32 receives the confirmed accident event from the FPGA and handles external communication.

```
FPGA
 ↓
ESP32
 ├──→ NEO-6M → GPS Location
 └──→ SIM800L → Emergency SMS
```

---

## 5. Accident Detection Flow

```text
Impact Detected
      ↓
250 ms Validation
      ↓
70% Criterion
      ↓
Acceleration + Speed Drop
      ↓
Accident Decision
      ↓
GPS Location
      ↓
GSM Emergency Alert
```

## 6. Development Requirements

### FPGA

* Xilinx Vivado
* Verilog HDL
* RTL simulator

### ESP32

* Arduino IDE
* ESP32 board support

## 7. Key Design Trade-off

**Advantage:** Deterministic FPGA-based accident processing with communication handled separately by the ESP32.

**Trade-off:** Additional hardware and greater system-design complexity.

